---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /next/
title: "The Thirty-Three — upcoming editions"
description: "The 33: a privately convened dinner for thirty-three guests, under Chatham House Rule. London, Davos, Lapland, Napa Valley, Barcelona and Mallorca."
---
{#
  The 33.

  Six squares, one per edition, built from the events table -- so announcing
  one is adding a row and swapping a photograph is editing a field, neither of
  which is a change to this template.

  A card is a button rather than a link: the editions have no pages of their
  own yet, and there is nowhere honest for a link to go. What it opens is the
  register-interest form with that edition already ticked, which is the one
  thing somebody looking at a photograph of Lapland wants to do next.
#}
<main id="main-content">

{# Where a form post lands when the script did not run. Shown by :target
   alone, so the one person who needs it -- the one with no JavaScript -- is
   the one it works for. #}
<div class="the33-thanks" id="registered" role="status">
  <div class="container">
    <p>Thank you &mdash; your interest has been registered. The programme chairs
    will be in touch.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="section the33-hero" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--rule">{{ upcomingCopy.eyebrow }}</p>
    <h1 class="the33-display" id="next-heading">
      {%- for line in upcomingCopy.heroLines -%}
        {%- if upcomingCopy.heroItalicLast and loop.last -%}
          <span><em>{{ line }}</em></span>
        {%- else -%}
          <span>{{ line }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <span>{{ upcomingCopy.heading }}</span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </h1>
    {% if upcomingCopy.heroLede %}
    <p class="the33-lede">{{ upcomingCopy.heroLede }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section the33-editions" aria-labelledby="editions-heading">
  <div class="container container--wide">
    <h2 class="the33-h2" id="editions-heading">{{ upcomingCopy.editionsHeading or "Upcoming Highlights" }}</h2>
    {% if upcomingCopy.standfirst %}
    <p class="the33-standfirst">{{ upcomingCopy.standfirst }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if events and events.upcoming and events.upcoming.length %}
    <div class="the33-cards">
      {% for event in events.upcoming %}
      {% set place = event.city or event.name %}
      <article class="the33-card reveal" data-edition="{{ event.slug }}"
               data-label="{{ place }} — {{ event.whenLabel }}"
               role="button" tabindex="0" aria-haspopup="dialog">
        {% if event.imagePath %}
        <img src="/assets/images/{{ event.imagePath }}" alt="{{ place }}"
             width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        {% endif %}
        <span class="the33-cue">{{ upcomingCopy.cue or "Register interest" }}</span>
        <span class="the33-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="the33-body">
          <span class="the33-when">{{ event.whenLabel }}</span>
          <p class="the33-place">{{ place }}</p>
          {% if event.tagline %}<p class="the33-blurb">{{ event.tagline }}</p>{% endif %}
        </div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% else %}
    {# Nothing announced yet. Saying so is better than an empty grid that looks
       like a fault. #}
    <p class="the33-none">Nothing is announced just yet. The next dates will appear here first.</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if upcomingCopy.footnote %}
    <p class="the33-closer">{{ upcomingCopy.footnote }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if upcomingCopy.credits %}
    <p class="the33-credits">{{ upcomingCopy.credits }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

{#
  The form.

  One dialog for all six, with the card you clicked ticked on the way in.
  Rendered here rather than built by script so that it is in the page for
  anybody whose JavaScript did not run: the noscript block above unhides it as
  an ordinary section, and it posts the same fields to the same endpoint.
#}
{# Without script the overlay is a hidden element and the form is unreachable,
   which would make the fallback endpoint pointless. This turns it into an
   ordinary section at the foot of the page instead. #}
<noscript>
  <style>
    .the33-overlay[hidden] { display: block; }
    .the33-overlay { position: static; padding: 0 0 64px; background: #111829; }
    .the33-dialog { margin: 0 auto; border: 0; }
    .the33-card { cursor: default; }
    .the33-cue { display: none; }
    /* The real checkbox does the work when nothing is drawing the square. */
    .the33-chip input { position: static; width: auto; height: auto; opacity: 1; }
    .the33-box { display: none; }
    .the33-close { display: none; }
  </style>
</noscript>

<div class="the33-overlay" id="the33-overlay" hidden>
  <div class="the33-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="the33-dlg-title">
    <button class="the33-close" id="the33-close" type="button" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>

    <form id="the33-form" method="post" action="/api/the-33" novalidate>
      <h3 id="the33-dlg-title">{{ upcomingCopy.formHeading or "Register your interest" }}</h3>
      {% if upcomingCopy.formLede %}
      <p class="the33-dialog-lede">{{ upcomingCopy.formLede }}</p>
      {% endif %}

      <div class="the33-field">
        <label for="the33-name">Full name</label>
        <input id="the33-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
      </div>
      <div class="the33-field">
        <label for="the33-email">Email</label>
        <input id="the33-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required>
      </div>
      <div class="the33-field">
        <label for="the33-company">Company</label>
        <input id="the33-company" name="company" type="text" autocomplete="organization" required>
      </div>

      <fieldset class="the33-picker">
        <legend class="the33-prompt">{{ upcomingCopy.pickerPrompt or "Please select the event you want to participate in" }}</legend>
        {% if upcomingCopy.pickerHint %}
        <p class="the33-hint">{{ upcomingCopy.pickerHint }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="the33-chips">
          {% for event in events.upcoming %}
          {% set place = event.city or event.name %}
          <label class="the33-chip" data-key="{{ event.slug }}">
            <input type="checkbox" name="editions" value="{{ place }} — {{ event.whenLabel }}">
            <span class="the33-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="the33-chip-text">{{ place }}<span class="the33-chip-when">{{ event.whenLabel }}</span></span>
          </label>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      {# The honeypot and the clock, the same two the invitation form uses. #}
      <div class="the33-trap" aria-hidden="true">
        <label for="the33-website">Website</label>
        <input id="the33-website" name="website" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
      </div>
      <input type="hidden" name="startedAt" id="the33-started" value="">
      <input type="hidden" name="source" value="the-33">

      <p class="the33-err" id="the33-err" role="alert" hidden></p>
      <button class="the33-submit" id="the33-submit" type="submit">Submit</button>
      {% if upcomingCopy.smallprint %}
      <p class="the33-smallprint">{{ upcomingCopy.smallprint }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </form>

    <div class="the33-done" id="the33-done" hidden>
      <h3>Thank you</h3>
      <p id="the33-done-msg"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</main>
